.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/*.sqlite
data/*.db
data/*.parquet
data/raw/
data/logs/

# Pre-built holdings snapshot IS committed, unlike the other data/*.db
# files (market.db price cache, seen_filings.db alert state) -- 82
# investors x 20 quarters takes long enough to fetch cold that a fresh
# Render/Streamlit Cloud deploy risks hitting the platform's request
# timeout via the in-app "fetch now" button. Shipping a working snapshot
# means the site is usable immediately; the sidebar button still refreshes
# it live whenever that's wanted.
!data/holdings.db

# Same reasoning for the CUSIP->ticker map: it's effectively static (a
# ticker rarely changes), but resolving it cold hits OpenFIGI's ~23
# req/min unauthenticated rate limit -- 5000+ CUSIPs across 82 investors
# x 20 quarters takes 10+ minutes on a fresh cache. Kept in its own file
# (not market.db) specifically so this can be committed WITHOUT also
# shipping market.db's "current price" snapshots, which go stale within
# days and would be actively misleading if committed as if fresh.
!data/tickers.db
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
